A WAL filename​ in PostgreSQL (e.g. 0000000300004B2900000087) has this internal binary/hex structure:
Part
	
Bytes
	
Description


1–8​
	
00000003
	
Timeline ID​ (e.g. 3)


9–12​
	
0000
	
usually zeros or part of upper LSN​


13–16​
	
4B29
	
Upper 32 bits of the LSN​ ✅


17–20​
	
0000
	

21–24​
	
0087
	
Lower 32 bits of the LSN​ ✅
